
Mid-Point Circle Drawing Algorithm – Theory

The Mid-Point Circle Drawing Algorithm is a raster graphics algorithm used to draw a circle on a pixel-based display. It determines the closest pixel position to form a smooth circle using only integer calculations. The algorithm is based on the circle equation:

x^2 + y^2 = r^2

Instead of floating-point arithmetic, it uses a decision parameter to choose the next pixel, making it fast and efficient for computer graphics applications.


