Basic Idea

The circle is drawn in the first octant starting from point .

For each calculated point, the corresponding seven symmetric points are plotted because a circle is symmetric about its axes and diagonals.

A decision parameter (d) is used to check which pixel is closer to the actual circle path and update the next pixel accordingly.



